{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5_bracket3_div_bracket6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5_bracket3_div_bracket6","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L201-L210","doc":"**Tau ratio presentation.** `[5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q = [5]_q / ([2]_q · (1 + h²))`.\nAs above, the non-vanishing hypotheses are an artefact of writing the\nidentity as a quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_halves_factor_eq_q_brackets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_halves_factor_eq_q_brackets","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L189-L199","doc":"**Muon ratio presentation.** `(3 + h²)/(2 + h²) = [3]_q · [2]_q / [4]_q`.\nOver a general field the quotient form needs both denominators\nnonzero (the equality is vacuous where `[4]_q` or `2 + h²` vanishes,\ne.g. char 2); the underlying identity\n`three_halves_factor_cross_mul` needs neither. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:three-halves-structural-factor","label":"prop:three-halves-structural-factor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.heckeH_mk0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.heckeH_mk0","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L181-L187","doc":"Bridge to the classical presentation: over a field, `Units.mk0`\nturns the earlier hypothesis `q ≠ 0` into the unit `q` used above,\nand the unit coercion `↑q⁻¹` is the field inverse `q⁻¹`. Nothing is\nlost by carrying `q : Kˣ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5_bracket3_cross_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5_bracket3_cross_mul","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L156-L168","doc":"**THEOREM (tau structural-factor reduction), division-free.** The\nconjectured tau closure factor `[5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q` reduces to\n`[5]_q / ([2]_q · (1 + h²))`; cross-multiplied,\n\n  [5]_q · [3]_q · ([2]_q · (1 + h²)) = [5]_q · [6]_q.\n\nHolds over any commutative ring. `bracket5_bracket3_div_bracket6`\nbelow recovers the quotient form over a field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket6_eq_bracket2_bracket3_times_one_plus_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket6_eq_bracket2_bracket3_times_one_plus_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L144-L154","doc":"**THEOREM (algebraic — tau structural).** [6]_q = [2]_q · [3]_q · (1 + h²).\nThe fundamental identity behind the tau closure\n`ξ_3 = [5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_halves_factor_cross_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_halves_factor_cross_mul","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L112-L127","doc":"**MAIN THEOREM (T6 gap (c) muon structural identity), division-free.**\nThe canonical lepton-mass-tower correction factor for the muon is\n`[3]_q · [2]_q / [4]_q`, with equivalent closed form\n`(3 + h²) / (2 + h²)`. Stated here as the cross-multiplied identity\n\n  (3 + h²) · [4]_q = [3]_q · [2]_q · (2 + h²)\n\nwhich is the content of the ratio equality and holds over **any**\ncommutative ring — no denominators, hence no non-vanishing\nhypotheses. `three_halves_factor_eq_q_brackets` below recovers the\nquotient form over a field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.two_plus_h_sq_times_bracket2_eq_bracket4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.two_plus_h_sq_times_bracket2_eq_bracket4","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L105-L110","doc":"**THEOREM (algebraic).** (2 + h²) · [2]_q = [4]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_plus_h_sq_eq_bracket3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.three_plus_h_sq_eq_bracket3","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**THEOREM (algebraic).** 3 + h² = [3]_q. Laurent identity over any\ncommutative ring; only `↑q * ↑q⁻¹ = 1` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket6","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L90-L93","doc":"q-bracket [6]_q = q⁵ + q³ + q + q⁻¹ + q⁻³ + q⁻⁵. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket5","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L86-L88","doc":"q-bracket [5]_q = q⁴ + q² + 1 + q⁻² + q⁻⁴. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket4","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L82-L84","doc":"q-bracket [4]_q = q³ + q + q⁻¹ + q⁻³. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket3","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L79-L80","doc":"q-bracket [3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.bracket2","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L76-L77","doc":"q-bracket [2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ThreeHalvesStructuralFactor.heckeH","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/three-halves-structural-factor.lean#L73-L74","doc":"Hecke amplitude h = q - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}